                                <span>Palette</span>
                                <select class="palette-select">
                                    <option value="clifford">Repo: blue → magenta</option>
                                    <option value="flow">Repo: turquoise → amber</option>
                                    <option value="ice">Extra: ice</option>
                                    <option value="ember">Extra: ember</option>
                                </select>
                            </label>
                            <label class="slider compact"><span>Glow <output data-for="glow">2</output></span><input type="range" data-key="glow" min="0" max="6" step="1" value="2" /></label>
                        </div>

                        <fieldset class="segmented">
                            <legend>Composition target</legend>
                            <label><input type="radio" name="target" value="desktop" checked /><span>Desktop 16:9</span></label>
                            <label><input type="radio" name="target" value="mobile" /><span>Phone 13:6</span></label>
                        </fieldset>

                        <label class="select">
                            <span>Output size (longest side)</span>
                            <select class="res-select">
                                <option value="1280">1280 px (CLI default)</option>
                                <option value="2048" class="large-res">2048 px (CLI maximum)</option>
                            </select>
                        </label>

                        <div class="action-row">
                            <button type="button" class="neon-btn download-btn">Download PNG</button>
                            <button type="button" class="ghost-btn copy-btn">Copy preset JSON</button>
                        </div>

                        <details class="json-panel">
                            <summary>Preset JSON for this design</summary>
                            <pre><code class="preset-json"></code></pre>
                        </details>
                    </form>
                </div>

                <div class="port-notes">
                    <article>
                        <h3>Exact: seeding</h3>
                        <p>
                            The page re-implements NumPy's <code>SeedSequence</code> and PCG64 generator, so a seed yields the same start
                            points as <code>np.random.default_rng(seed)</code>.
                        </p>
                        <p class="rng-check" aria-live="polite">Checking the RNG port…</p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>Faithful: the maths</h3>
                        <p>
                            Same recurrence, same normalised vector field, same
                            bounding-box framing (12% / 9% margins), colour ramps,
                            dimmed glow and stroke widths as the Python compositor.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>Approximate: the pixels</h3>
                        <p>
                            JavaScript's <code>sin</code>/<code>cos</code> can
                            differ from C's in the last bit, and the attractor is
                            chaotic, so individual points drift while the shape
                            stays the same. Canvas lines are anti-aliased; Pillow's
                            are not. This is a port, not the Python engine.
                        </p>
                    </article>
                </div>
