                            <figcaption>
                                <strong>{preview.name}</strong>
                                <span class="mono">{preview.meta}</span>
                                <span class="score">Manual AQS review: {preview.score}/100 · “Refine”</span>
                            </figcaption>
                        </figure>
                    ))}
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="mw-how">
                <div class="section-heading">
                    <p class="eyebrow">03 — How it works</p>
                    <h2 id="mw-how">Presets in, deterministic pixels out.</h2>
                    <p>
                        A design is a small JSON preset. The CLI validates it,
                        generates points with a seeded engine, and the
                        compositor frames and draws them on a true-black canvas.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <ol class="pipeline" aria-label="Generation pipeline">
                    <li><span>1</span><strong>Preset JSON</strong><small>presets.py validates the schema</small></li>
                    <li><span>2</span><strong>Seeded engine</strong><small>attractors.py · flow_fields.py</small></li>
                    <li><span>3</span><strong>Compositor</strong><small>framing, colour ramp, glow</small></li>
                    <li><span>4</span><strong>PNG</strong><small>exclusive write, never overwrites</small></li>
                </ol>

