                    <article class="panel">
                        <h3>Validated presets</h3>
                        <p>Every preset must carry these fields before anything is generated:</p>
                        <dl class="rule-list">
                            {validationRules.map((rule) => (
                                <div>
                                    <dt><code>{rule.field}</code></dt>
                                    <dd>{rule.rule}</dd>
                                </div>
                            ))}
                        </dl>
                    </article>

                    <article class="panel">
                        <h3>Workload budgets</h3>
                        <p>
                            Each preset declares a <code>preview</code> and a <code>final</code> budget,
                            and each engine applies
                            its own tighter limits <em>before</em> allocating
                            arrays, so a typo cannot ask for a billion points.
                        </p>
                        <div class="limit-grid">
                            {engineLimits.map((limit) => (
                                <div>
                                    <strong>{limit.value}</strong>
                                    <span>{limit.label}</span>
                                </div>
                            ))}
                        </div>
                        <p class="small">
                            The compositor separately caps previews at
                            3840 × 2160 pixels and 1,000,000 drawn points.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article class="panel code-panel">
                        <h3>The attractor, verbatim</h3>
                        <p>
                            From <code>src/mathwall/attractors.py</code>. A
                            local NumPy generator seeds the start point; every
                            step is checked for non-finite output.
                        </p>
                        <pre class="code"><code>{codeExcerpt}</code></pre>
                    </article>

                    <article class="panel">
                        <h3>Determinism, by design</h3>
                        <ul class="tick-list">
                            <li>No global randomness: <code>np.random.default_rng(seed)</code> per call.</li>
                            <li>Same preset and seed → identical points and identical pixels, asserted in tests.</li>
                            <li>Untouched background pixels must be exactly <code>(0, 0, 0)</code> for OLED panels.</li>
                            <li>Exact dependency versions locked in <code>uv.lock</code>.</li>
                            <li>The CLI refuses to overwrite an existing file, including its own preset.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

